A||||22||RossT||have you had a close call (accident) in your fiero?||||1||
Z||000000||RossT||02-04-2000||05:03 PM||||There has been alot of posting lately about fiero involved in accidents.  But what about those close calls?  You know.. the near misses that get your heart pounding in a split second (that seems like minutes), and you luck out.. no damage..<P>mine goes as follows:  I bought my first fiero last May.  My nice 88gt was stashed away in the gararge. About a week later we had a massive thunder storm come thru, with lots of gail force winds.  I had a heavey extension ladder mounted on the wall next to the fiero.  Well you guessed it. I heard a loud crash during the storm, when into the gararge to see what had took place. All I saw was the ladder sticking out from behind the fiero.  It took me two weeks to get the nerve up to check for damage. There was know way it could miss.  Well it did.. by about 1/2 inch.. it was a miracle. <P>lets hear your near miss.||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||02-04-2000||05:11 PM||||It was really weird. So weird that I told my wife about it. I had this feeling that I was going to be in an accident. I had been in 3 in 6 years, none of them my fault so I figure I started to get the feel for them.<BR>    Anyway Im on pins and needles for 2 days, driving defensively but not really being at ease. Then one day on the freeway it happened. My wife was driving her Fiero behind me and I was in the slow lane when this huge truck loaded down with wheel rims come barreling onto the freeway and starts in on my lane while Im in it. I saw him coming on and I don't even remember downshifting but my passenger window was filled with nothing but truck. I glanced at my sideview mirror and prayed nobody was in my blindspot and just gunned the hell out of that lane. My wife was freaked. She saw the truck come so close that she beleived that the truck physically crashed me into the other lane. I pulled off at the next offramp and we got something to eat just to stay off the roads for a while but I felt like the weight had been lifted. I haven't ignored a feeling since.||||reg||4
Z||000002||wkayl||02-04-2000||07:57 PM||||My son wasn't so lucky.  But he was able to drive away.  Check here to see what a car running a stopsign will do to a 1984 SE: <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/wkayl/crash.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/wkayl/crash.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||02-04-2000||08:10 PM||||I almost hit a curb in the snow but pumped the brakes to stop, does that count?||||reg||1
Z||000004||daved||02-04-2000||09:25 PM||||I had my 86GT a couple of months and was on my way home, you know, one of those filthy dark rainy nights with no moon.  Exited the freeway, and turned left over the bridge. Got up to about 70km/hr as I came over the brow of the bridge, only to see a transport, obviously having no intention of stopping, exiting from the other direction. I was presented with the full side of the trailer (can the Fiero pass underneath?), or the ditch. Laid on the anchors as if my life depended on it (and it did!) Wow, what a suprise; she hauled down to a few kliks just as I approached the curb, and I was able to steer around the rear of the trailer.  I can tell you that I was suitably impressed at the Fiero's ability to stop in awful conditions, and its manoeuverability. I can testify that the brakes are adequate, and the BF Goodrich T/A tires are impressive.  Glad I didn't hit anything.  <BR>Moral of the story...don't accelerate quite so fast over those bridges (any more).  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||kel||02-04-2000||11:30 PM||||wkayl,<BR>I'm glad to hear your son was not hurt worse than he was.  He must have had a guardian angel watching over him that day!  Just looking at those pictures makes you think of what "could" have happened.||||reg||1
Z||000006||wkayl||02-05-2000||12:42 AM||||Thx Kel<BR>It's better to have your son standing in your bedroom at 1:15 in the morning telling you that a guy just smashed his car than getting a phone call!!  Also, he loves his 86 GT he got with some of the insurance money.  We just got a letter fron the courts today asking us what our losses were. They may make the other kid pay restitution for what his insurance didn't cover (we had new engine, tires, windshield and a/c).||||reg||1
Z||000007||86SE||02-05-2000||02:09 AM||||About a month and a half ago I was driving on Ice and floored my V-6 and spun a cookie and flew over some train tracks (side ways) and came to a hault at about a 50 degree angle in the ditch!!  I almost rolled it!!<P>Ahhh, but now its parked safe in my garage.......||||reg||1
Z||000008||kel||02-05-2000||02:09 AM||||wkayl,<BR>I have a 20 yr. old son and about 3 years ago, I got a phone call from him saying he had been in an accident.  He was pretty shook up, but fortunately no one was hurt.  (I however aged about 5 years)<BR>I'm sure Casey will enjoy his 86 GT.  Fieros are definitely addictive!   ||||reg||1
Z||000009||wkayl||02-05-2000||11:31 PM||||I got my 86GT in June of '99.  It had 75,000 miles and completly original.  <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/wkayl/cars.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/wkayl/cars.html</A> <BR> My wife didn't know I was getting one until I parked it in front of the house all paid for (and I'm still married).  To soften the blow, I let her drive it to work the next few days.  After the second day she said she wasn't sure she wanted to drive it again.  On the way to work, she saw a full size Chev Blazer start backing out of a driveway looking like it wasn't going to stop.  She hit the breaks just as it passed in front of her WITHOUT A DRIVER!!  It went across the road into the ditch and hit the fence on the other side.||||reg||1
Z||000010||87GT||02-06-2000||10:31 AM||||Its funny you should post a topic about accidents.  On February 2nd, I had come to a stop at a red light.  I was sitting behind a car listening to my tunes when I looked in my rear view mirror and noticed this black Jeep coming awefully fast.  I couldnt go anywhere and I had a feeling this person wasnt going to be able to stop, so I put in the clutch and let of the break so my 87GT wouldnt absord a harder hit.  Anyways, this person slams the break and hits the back of my car.  I WAS PISSED!  I got out in the middle of a pretty high traffic area to look at my car, the woman didnt even get out of her Jeep.  I looked at my bumper and was shocked not to see any damage at all.  It hit hard too.  Anyways, I pointed at her and told her she was, "Damn lucky!"  Later that day I took a closer look at where she hit and I can see that she spider webbed the paint a little, but not much.  My bumper needs to be repainted anyways.  So thats my story.  My baby was okay and it wasnt a hard enough hit to hurt me so everything is okay.  Its hell out there!||||reg||8
Z||000011||Monkeyman||02-06-2000||06:31 PM||||I wasn't driving and it wasn't my Fiero, but here goes.  WT III and I were the last car in line at the recent Ohio meet.  I was pointing something out to him about stereos (I'll take 1/2 of the blame) and we looked up in time to see everyone else just about stopped and turning left into Ft. Ancient.  WT III locked em up and pulled into the next lane (smart idea) and we came to a stop before any damage was done.  Whew!  It's a good thing he really is a good driver.  That was the only incident we had the entire trip.||||reg||1
Z||000012||DJRice||02-07-2000||10:18 AM||||I have one, but I wasnt in a car at the time.<BR>Two weeks before Christmas, My aunt and uncle, my cousin and her two daughters came over from Louisana to my parents house in FL.  One Saturday afternoon, my aunt, cousin, and mother wanted to go shopping, so I volunteered to chauffer (sp?) them into Jacksonville for a lunch and shopping trip.  My mother had a hip replacement a while back and although she can walk with a walker, when we go shopping we use a wheelchair just because thats the safest right now.  <BR>Anyway, we had just finished lunch and were getting in the car.  Everyone else was in the car and I was folding up my moms wheelchair and loading it in the trunk.  There was a Saturn in the parking spot opposite ours that was backing out.  So hes backing up and I'm only watching him out of the corner of my as I fold the wheelchair up.  Next thing I know I am pinned between a Saturn pressing against the wheelchair and a Lincoln Towncar.  I started screaming "Hey Hey Stop Stop Stop" and I started beating on the guys trunk lid.  So He finally stopped and eased forward so I could get out from between the wheelchair and car.  The dude gets out of the car and he was white as a ghost because he realized that he had just hit some guy (6'3" 215 lbs) loading a wheelchair in a handicap parking spot.  If my mother had not been standing right there (after she heard me hollar and then felt the car move) I would have cursed that guy up and down after I gave him a good ol right to the grill, but I decided that since I was so glad not to be hurt and since and my mom was already upset I told the guy to be more careful, have a merry christmas, and get going before I changed my mind.<P>Now I know I could/should have called the cops and probably taken him to court, maybe even gotten some money, but it didnt seem like the thing to do at the time becuase the worst thing that happened was he upset my mother.<P>So thats my close call...||||reg||1
Z||000013||ChadMan||02-07-2000||10:59 AM||||Once I was driving down a two-lane road in my 84 when I came to a line of stopped traffic.  A road crew was repairing one lane and flagmen were letting traffic take turns using the one good lane.  Our flagman turned his sign from "STOP" to "SLOW" and the line of traffic began to move at about 15 mph.  The flagman had his back to traffic as the van in front of me passed by.  <P>Would you believe that as I drove by, this dumb SOB takes a big step backward and runs into the side of my car with his a$$?  As he planted his big fat plumber's butt on my window/door, my Fiero spun him around and he sprawled in the road.  The car behind me stopped quickly so as not to hit this moron.  I looked around, noticed none of the construction workers had seen what happened, and made a quick decision to get the hell out of there.<P>I knew I was in the right, but was worried that John Law wouldn't see it the same way (gee - a guy in a red sports car hits a construction worker.  Who do you suppose will get cited?)  I spent the afternoon buffing Bubba-butt scratches out of my finish.  I normally wouldn't advocate hit-and-run, but I saved myself a big fat insurance claim that day!||||reg||1
Z||000014||bHooper||02-07-2000||01:16 PM||||i have a story very similar to 87GT's... in '91 and '92 i was living in st petersburg florida and working in tampa.  everymorning i had to drive accross the howard franklin bridge (also know as the frankenstein, and about 8 miles long).  one morning, trafic came to a quick stop. as i was sitting there, in the middle of the bridge, i saw a integra coming up fast behind me... well he bumped me hard enough to pop the rear view mirror into my lap (it was always lose).  well we didn't stop to get out, just let it go and all i wound up with was a spider web on the bumper.||||reg||1
Z||000015||stsmithgt||02-07-2000||03:35 PM||||I have to stop reading these things.  It's reminding me of the lady who spidered the nose of my GT.  It was also a coincedence that she didn't speak english.  I spelling may be bad, but I know the rules on the road.  Her passenger crack the windshield of that car, which didn't even belong to her.  I bet she wasn't even covered by the guys insurance too.  She needs to learn how to merge into moving traffic that !@#$#@@#$#@#$%^!!!! Ahhhh, that feels better. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000016||DRH||02-07-2000||03:45 PM||||People that think they should STOP and look at the end of a freeway on ramp before merging... AAARRRGGG!!! Why do they think they make them a quarter mile long???<P>Never hit one... but had to take the emergency lane a few times! <P>Your right... it does feel better  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 02-07-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000017||FieroMorg||02-07-2000||03:56 PM||||3 years ago my brother got in a big car accident in my mom's Fiero(84 SE).  He hit a 18 wheeler going.....well... very fast (speedo was stuck at 140 kmph).  He hit the back of the truck on the drivers side(I guess he was swerving around to avoid the truck) and ended up rolling the car 4 or 5 times util he ended up in a farmers field next to the road.  Luckily a helicopter was in the area on a cancelled call and he was quickly rushed to the hospital with a ruptured spleen, 4 broken ribs, and a punctured lung. The car was a total write off(his hadprints were still on the steering wheel), it was only about 2 feet tall when it was said and done.  Luckily he survived, and to this day my parents still can't believe that he made it through. A true test of Fiero Crash Saftey! 2 weeks later I bought my first Fiero, and I haven't looked back ever since!    <p>[This message has been edited by FieroMorg (edited 02-08-2000).]||||reg||14
